<title>BELGIUM: EU postpones nickel decision for euro coins.</title>
<headline>EU postpones nickel decision for euro coins.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union finance ministers took no decision on Monday on the nickel content of future euro coins but said they would wait for proposals from the European Commission, EU diplomats said.</p>
<p>The ministers discussed whether the new coins should be multi-sided and how much nickel, if any, there should be in them. &quot;There was no final agreement these two points,&quot; one diplomat said.  </p>
<p>Sweden had been seeking to reduce the nickel content as far as possible in the planned coins because of health reasons, saying it can cause allergic reactions.</p>
<p>Vending machine operators have also expressed worries about the effect of multi-sided coins on their business.</p>
<p>Diplomats said it would be some months before the Commission came up with proposals.</p>
</text>
